 "text": "A year ago, I began volunteering at a food bank near my home. I go there every Saturday morning for three hours. My job is to sort the food that people donate. I check the dates, group the items and pack them into boxes for families. The work is simple, but it matters. Each box helps a family through a difficult week. I have also met many kind people who give their time in the same way. If you want to help, start with one morning a month. Small amounts of time, given regularly, make a real difference. You do not need special skills, only a little time and some patience."
